; BirchTree — 4th Forest tree pick, added 2026-08-26 (content-variety pass, Task 5). A
; genuinely different silhouette from the 3 existing picks (CommonTree1/2's round canopy,
; PineTree's narrow tapered conifer): thin trunk, light/sparse canopy — the "birch" read.
;
; Source: "BirchTree_1.fbx", Ultimate Nature Pack by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal —
; License.txt at `source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../License.txt` re-checked
; before import, per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate (states CC0 1.0 Universal /
; Public Domain Dedication, same boilerplate as every other Quaternius pack in this repo).
; Recorded in project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres (extends
; that pack's existing assets_used list — same pack already used for Rock_1/Den pieces).
;
; SCALE: the source file bakes a 90-degree axis correction + scale=100 into its own child
; node (Blender Z-up -> glTF/FBX Y-up, same mechanism PineTree.tscn's header documents),
; measured post-correction global AABB height = 3.5738 units (footprint ~1.702 x 2.480 at
; that height) — scaled here by 0.700 to hit the SAME ~2.5-tile canopy-height target
; CommonTree1/CommonTree2/PineTree all use, so height stays a control variable and only
; the silhouette changes between variants. FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD number —
; FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, same open question every prior tree variant carries (whether
; matched-height reads correctly at the fixed ~45 camera pitch, vs. a deliberately
; taller/shorter alternative).
;
; SLAB IS 1.0x0.2x1.0 (matches every current-generation terrain slab, post the
; "SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0" cross-tile seam fix PineTree.tscn's header documents).
;
; FLOOR TREATMENT MATCHES COMMONTREE1/COMMONTREE2/PINETREE EXACTLY (same slab tint, same
; 3-patch moss/litter blotch treatment, same relative transforms) so a Forest tile's floor
; reads identically regardless of which of the now-4 trees it lands on.
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (required, not cosmetic): identical
; OcclusionFader exemption requirement as every sibling terrain scene — see
; CommonTree1.tscn's header for the full mechanism. The ground plane (renamed "Ground")
; and all 3 floor patches are children of a wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab".
